1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,978
Half-time in Mostar. Zrinjski, nil.

2
00:00:06,448 --> 00:00:10,017
AZ Alkmaar … three.

3
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:15,157
Forty-five minutes later, it was the
greatest night a club from Bosnia and

4
00:00:15,197 --> 00:00:17,945
Herzegovina had ever had in Europe.

5
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:22,077
Luka Modrić played for Zrinjski as a
teenager.

6
00:00:22,227 --> 00:00:23,991
He once put it like this.

7
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:28,636
This is the story of the night Zrinjski
proved it.

8
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:35,480
No club from Bosnia and Herzegovina had
ever played a group-stage match in

9
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,598
Europe. Not one.

10
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:43,590
Zrinjski got past Breiðablik, lost to
LASK, and dropped into the Conference

11
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:49,384
League. Group E. Aston Villa. Legia
Warsaw.

12
00:00:49,714 --> 00:00:50,826
And AZ.

13
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:55,097
That afternoon, the storm clouds sat on
the mountains.

14
00:00:55,427 --> 00:00:58,680
The stalls were open hours before
kick-off.

15
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:02,742
The team bus rolled in behind the main
stand.

16
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:06,621
On the merchandise table, one shirt said
it all.

17
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:10,228
They call the ground Pod Bijelim Brijegom.

18
00:01:10,378 --> 00:01:12,824
The Stadium under the White Hill.

19
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:16,189
Five thousand, one hundred inside.

20
00:01:16,519 --> 00:01:20,078
Most of them had waited their whole lives
for this.

21
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:24,927
And across the halfway line … AZ Alkmaar.

22
00:01:25,257 --> 00:01:29,357
Semi-finalists in this competition the
season before.

23
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:35,352
Before kick-off, one model gave Zrinjski a
thirty-four per cent chance of

24
00:01:35,392 --> 00:01:38,395
winning. The exact score that was coming?

25
00:01:38,725 --> 00:01:40,580
One in two hundred.

26
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:45,726
Quick one, before we go on. If you've ever
stood in the rain for ninety minutes

27
00:01:45,766 --> 00:01:48,657
and called it a good day, you belong here.

28
00:01:48,807 --> 00:01:53,843
Subscribe to FanLife Football Stories, and
take your place on the terrace.

29
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:57,742
Kick-off, under the floodlights.

30
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:02,050
Ten minutes. Myron van Brederode.

31
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,494
Nil–one.

32
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:08,463
Thirty-two. Sven Mijnans. Nil–two.

33
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:14,027
Forty-four. Dani de Wit … Nil–three.

34
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:20,284
Half-time. Nil–three. Down at the food

35
00:02:20,324 --> 00:02:24,442
stalls, under the floodlights, people
stood and ate and said very little.

36
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:30,595
Their first ever night in a European
group, and it was over before it began.

37
00:02:31,065 --> 00:02:32,781
Everybody knew it.

38
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:36,959
Everybody … except one man on the bench.

39
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:41,590
Krunoslav Rendulić made one change.

40
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:46,695
Andrija Balić off. Zvonimir Kožulj on.

41
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,560
Two minutes later, a free kick.

42
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,725
Thirty metres out.

43
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:54,975
Kožulj … Over the wall. In.

44
00:02:55,380 --> 00:03:00,617
The first goal a Bosnian club had ever
scored in a European group stage.

45
00:03:01,017 --> 00:03:03,634
And something in the stand changed.

46
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:07,740
Sixty-eight. Josip Ćorluka. Two–three.

47
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:12,383
Seventy-one. Aldin Hrvanović, from outside
the box.

48
00:03:12,423 --> 00:03:13,509
Three–three!

49
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:16,296
Three goals in twenty-three minutes.

50
00:03:16,336 --> 00:03:18,369
The White Hill was shaking.

51
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:22,426
Eighty-one. Matija Malekinušić …

52
00:03:22,826 --> 00:03:27,623
the post. The ball falls to Zvonimir
Kožulj.

53
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,076
Four–three!

54
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:33,971
Nil–three at half-time. Four–three at the
end.

55
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,975
And when the whistle went, Mostar sang.

56
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:41,979
In the other dressing room, there was
nothing to sing.

57
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:45,837
The AZ coach, Pascal Jansen, that night.

58
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:51,949
AZ became the first Dutch club ever to
lose a European match after leading by

59
00:03:51,989 --> 00:03:52,732
three goals.

60
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:57,476
In Belgium, they called it a rollercoaster
nobody had ever seen.

61
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:00,783
The Dutch football magazine did not spare
them.

62
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:06,115
Two months later, Jansen was asked if he
had slept after Mostar.

63
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:10,259
In Mostar, nobody was sleeping either.

64
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,936
Rendulić, on the phone that night.

65
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:18,769
Zvonimir Kožulj, on at half-time, was
named the best player of the round.

66
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:22,839
And Bosnia’s own federation wrote it down
for history.

67
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:29,345
It did not last. At Villa Park they lost
to a goal in stoppage time.

68
00:04:29,815 --> 00:04:32,173
Zrinjski finished fourth.

69
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:36,388
But nobody in Mostar remembers the table.

70
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:40,457
They remember half-time. Nil–three.

71
00:04:40,857 --> 00:04:43,182
And the forty-five minutes after it.

72
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:48,826
Every match in this film is waiting in the
FanLife archive, with the games, the

73
00:04:48,866 --> 00:04:51,429
trivia and the stories of the whole club.

74
00:04:51,579 --> 00:04:55,551
Come and play it at fanlife.dubelteam.com.

75
00:04:55,701 --> 00:05:00,587
And if this story was yours too,
subscribe, and the next one will find you.
